ethercat-dkms for Debian
------------------------

Module identity: dkms module "ethercat", version equal to the upstream
package version (for example 1.6.9+4+g46cc20e6, derived from
debian/changelog). This intentionally differs from the development
wrapper MODULE_VERSION (1.6.9) recorded in configure/CONFIG_MODULE of
the packaging repository.

dkms_tree relocation: the dkms.conf forces
abs_builddir=/var/lib/dkms/ethercat/<version>/build to keep
cross-kernel builds inside the DKMS tree (the upstream build system
bakes this path at configure time). A relocated dkms_tree re-opens the
build escape and requires a regenerated dkms.conf.

Accepted build cost: the upstream top-level Kbuild compiles the
examples/ modules on every DKMS build although this package never
ships them; upstream exposes no gate. A future example-module compile
failure on a new kernel fails the whole DKMS build - report it against
the packaging repository.

